   "ruling": "Ruling: scope; the reviewer is right that f8582's passive activities carry no prior-year ownership condition, but each activity begun in 2025 is screened where it is entered: a Schedule C business in which the filer did not materially participate is refused by sc.screened (sc.passive false; i1040sc p. 4, Line G, the seven tests), a farm or a K-1 by scope.schedule1 (scope.farm, scope.k1), and a rental of real property is now computed with its passive loss limit (Schedule E with Form 8582, this merge: f8582, rental.active). The gated question catches what those do not: a passive activity owned before 2025 with prior-year unallowed losses or a 2025 disposition, the case its wording (no longer 'or rental') names. As in the landing render ruling, now with rentals computed rather than refused. Project stands.",
